<p>Resource goal: claim beginner rewards but do not burn premium currency or speedups randomly.</p>
<p>Common mistake: playing side systems before you know what the next Camp level requires.</p>
<h3>Step 2: Complete daily activity 200 every day</h3>
<p>Daily activity 200 is both an offer/task signal in researched versions and a core source of progression rewards. Treat it as your daily minimum. Log in, collect idle production, spend AP before it caps, claim guild gifts, use guild help, gather resources, restart research, and finish daily tasks.</p>
<p>Progress goal: never miss daily activity during a serious run.</p>
<p>Resource goal: stack speedups, resource chests, AP items, guild rewards, and event progress.</p>
<p>Common mistake: skipping daily activity because the rewards feel small. Over 20-30 days, missed dailies become missed milestones.</p>
<h3>Step 3: Reach Camp 6</h3>
<p>Camp 6 should be a tutorial-speed target. Upgrade only required Camp blockers. If a building is not required for Camp progress, ignore it unless the tutorial forces it.</p>
<p>Progress goal: clear tutorial/build requirements fast and get into a guild.</p>
<p>Resource goal: use only tiny speedups if they help meet the 24-hour style deadline.</p>
<p>Common mistake: trying to make the base balanced instead of rushing Camp requirements.</p>
<h3>Step 4: Reach Camp 13</h3>
<p>This is the first meaningful checkpoint. Start using the Camp screen as your task list. Write down or screenshot required buildings, then do those and nothing else. Begin Construction / Development research and ask for guild help before using speedups.</p>
<p>Progress goal: reach Camp 13 around the early timeline while preserving bigger speedups.</p>
<p>Resource goal: combine idle production, gathering, daily activity, events, guild gifts, and code/check-in rewards.</p>
<p>Common mistake: spending speedups on short timers that would finish naturally.</p>
<h3>Step 5: Reach Camp 16</h3>
<p>By Camp 16, queue discipline is everything. Always start the longest required upgrade before sleep. Keep research active. Send squads gathering when offline. If you are open to spending, this is where extra builder capacity starts to matter more than random packs.</p>
<p>Progress goal: keep builders active with no long idle gaps.</p>
<p>Resource goal: use speedups only when they unblock required Camp progress.</p>
<p>Common mistake: letting a builder sit idle overnight or while you are at work.</p>
<h3>Step 6: Reach Camp 18-20</h3>
<p>Camp 18 is where the offer starts feeling like a real builder grind. Camp 20 is a strong checkpoint for free and low-spend users. Resource requirements, build timers, and speedup decisions become more important.</p>
<p>Progress goal: complete daily activity 200, use guild help, and keep long upgrades running.</p>
<p>Resource goal: build a stockpile of construction speedups and resource chests for the low 20s.</p>
<p>Common mistake: burning saved resources as soon as you get them instead of holding for long Camp blockers.</p>
<h3>Step 7: Reassess at Camp 20-22</h3>
<p>Do not blindly continue. Check three things: did earlier milestones credit, how much time is left, and how much payout remains? If tracking is broken, this is where you should become cautious.</p>
<p>Progress goal: decide whether Camp 22/24 is still worth chasing.</p>
<p>Resource goal: save large speedups for required blockers only.</p>
<p>Common mistake: spending to chase higher milestones before confirming early credits.</p>
