<h2>Best No-Spend Strategy</h2>
<p>Your free path depends on consistency, not nonstop play. You need short, purposeful check-ins throughout the day.</p>
<p>Daily no-spend loop:</p>
<p>Claim idle production.</p>
<p>Complete daily activity 200.</p>
<p>Spend natural AP before it caps.</p>
<p>Claim guild gifts and guild aid.</p>
<p>Restart construction.</p>
<p>Restart research.</p>
<p>Send squads gathering.</p>
<p>Claim event rewards.</p>
<p>Save speedups for required Camp blockers.</p>
<p>Queue long upgrades before sleeping.</p>
<p>The goal is to make time work for you. Every idle builder, capped resource, unused AP bar, or idle gathering squad is lost progress.</p>
<h2>Where Free Resources Come From</h2>
<h3>Idle production</h3>
<p>Your base produces resources over time. Claim frequently enough that storage does not cap. If your production caps overnight, you lost free materials.</p>
<h3>Daily activity 200</h3>
<p>This should be your daily minimum. It helps with offer progress and generates recurring resources/speedups.</p>
<h3>Map gathering</h3>
<p>Gathering is one of the best free habits. Send squads before you log off, before bed, and any time you will be away.</p>
<h3>Guild gifts and guild aid</h3>
<p>A stronger guild means more help, more gifts, more rally/boss activity, and more chances at rewards. Even if you are free-to-play, guild activity can subsidize your progress.</p>
<h3>Events</h3>
<p>Events are where free players can punch above their weight. If a speedup, AP, gathering, or resource event window is active, batch your actions inside that window instead of spreading them randomly.</p>
<h3>Redeem codes</h3>
<p>Current code sources regularly mention rewards like Pallite, Lumber chests, Steel chests, AP, XP, and 5-minute speedups. Codes expire, so check active codes before starting. Do not list old codes as guaranteed evergreen rewards unless you verify them on starting.</p>
<h3>Official web store check-in</h3>
<p>The official Lilith web store check-in has shown daily rewards such as Pallite, 1-minute building speedups, and Palmon eggs. These are small but useful because no-spend runs are won by stacking small advantages.</p>
<h3>Research and construction bonuses</h3>
<p>Construction / Development research reduces the long-term pressure. It may not feel exciting, but any permanent build-time reduction compounds across the entire offer.</p>
<h2>What to Spend Free Resources On</h2>
<p>Spend resources in this order:</p>
<p>Required Camp buildings.</p>
<p>Construction / Development research.</p>
<p>Storage or production only if required by the Camp path.</p>
<p>Progression blockers that unlock the next required building.</p>
<p>Combat only if it directly blocks progression.</p>
<p>Everything else last.</p>
<p>Do not spend heavily on random combat upgrades, creature power, nice-to-have buildings, cosmetics, side systems, or short timers that would finish naturally.</p>
<h2>Pallite Strategy for No-Spend Players</h2>
<p>Pallite is a premium-style resource. Do not spend it emotionally. For offerwall purposes, Pallite is most useful when it shortens Camp progress.</p>
<p>Better uses:</p>
<ul>
<li>Construction speedups.</li>
<li>VIP or shop paths that unlock building speedups if available.</li>
<li>Emergency final blocker only if the milestone payout justifies it.</li>
<li>Event windows where spending Pallite also earns bonus rewards.</li>
</ul>
<p>Worse uses:</p>
<ul>
<li>Random summons.</li>
<li>Combat vanity.</li>
<li>Low-impact packs.</li>
<li>Short timers.</li>
<li>Anything bought before tracking is confirmed.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Speedup Strategy for Free Players</h2>
<p>Speedups are your most important free currency.</p>
<p>Use speedups on required Camp buildings, long upgrades, deadline-sensitive blockers, Camp upgrade timers, and event-timed building pushes. Avoid using speedups on short timers, optional buildings, combat upgrades, or anything that does not unlock the next Camp level.</p>
<p>Always request guild help before using speedups. Official/social tips and community advice repeatedly point to guild aid before speedups as a simple way to save time.</p>
<h2>Best Free Milestone Plan</h2>
<h3>Camp 6</h3>
<p>Push tutorial and required buildings only. Do not get distracted by side systems.</p>
<h3>Camp 13</h3>
<p>This is your first real payout target. Keep construction active, join a guild, and start saving bigger speedups.</p>
<h3>Camp 16</h3>
<p>Strong no-spend target. Focus on queue discipline and Construction / Development research.</p>
<h3>Camp 18</h3>
<p>Resource pressure begins. Use more check-ins, gather offline, and stop spending resources on optional upgrades.</p>
<h3>Camp 20</h3>
<p>Best realistic stretch target for many free players. This is a good place to reassess tracking and time left.</p>
<h3>Camp 22</h3>
<p>Possible for strong free runs, but do not assume it. You need saved speedups, active guild help, and no wasted upgrades.</p>
<h3>Camp 24+</h3>
<p>Treat as risky without spending. The opportunity cost and timer pressure become severe.</p>
<h2>Free Daily Schedule</h2>
<p>Morning:</p>
<ul>
<li>Claim idle production.</li>
<li>Restart builders.</li>
<li>Use guild aid.</li>
<li>Restart research.</li>
<li>Send squads gathering.</li>
</ul>
<p>Midday:</p>
<ul>
<li>Spend AP before cap.</li>
<li>Finish daily activity tasks.</li>
<li>Check events and guild rewards.</li>
<li>Start any finished required building.</li>
</ul>
<p>Evening:</p>
<ul>
<li>Push remaining daily activity 200.</li>
<li>Use speedups only if they block a required milestone.</li>
<li>Start the longest required upgrade before sleep.</li>
<li>Send squads gathering overnight.</li>
</ul>
<h2>No-Spend Mistakes That Kill Runs</h2>
<ul>
<li>Trying to max the offer for free.</li>
<li>Missing daily activity 200.</li>
<li>Joining a weak guild and staying there.</li>
<li>Spending speedups too early.</li>
<li>Upgrading every available building.</li>
<li>Letting builders sit idle.</li>
<li>Ignoring Construction / Development research.</li>
<li>Not gathering while offline.</li>
<li>Opening resource chests too early and wasting over-cap resources.</li>
<li>Not screenshotting milestones.</li>
<li>Continuing after tracking fails.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Should You Spend Anything?</h2>
<p>If your goal is a pure no-spend guide, the answer is no: build around Camp 13-20 and protect profit. If you are open to low spend, only buy efficiency: extra builder capacity, construction reduction, or purchase tasks that are directly reimbursed by the offer. Do not spend if early milestones have not tracked.</p>
<p>A good rule: if a purchase does not reduce build time, unlock a required queue, or trigger an offer milestone, it probably does not belong in an offerwall run.</p>
<h2>FAQ</h2>
<h3>Can I complete Palmon Survival without spending?</h3>
<p>You can complete some milestones without spending. Camp 13-20 is the realistic range for many free players. Camp 26-30 is not a realistic free-to-play plan for most users.</p>
<h3>What is the best no-spend milestone?</h3>
<p>Camp 16-20 is the best realistic target zone. Camp 22 is a stretch.</p>
<h3>Should I use redeem codes?</h3>
<p>Yes, but verify active codes on starting. Codes can provide Pallite, resource chests, AP, and speedups, but they expire or rotate.</p>
<h3>What should I do with Pallite?</h3>
<p>Use it for construction-related progress, VIP/shop paths that unlock speedups, or emergency blockers. Avoid random summons or combat vanity.</p>
<h3>Is it worth starting if I will not spend?</h3>
<p>Yes, if you are comfortable with partial completion. No, if your only goal is the max headline payout.</p>
